 "text": "Recorder of Deeds – Howell County Missouri\nCall on : 417-256-2591\nHours : Mon-Fri 8:30 - 4:30pm\nHowell County Missouri\nHome\nCities & Towns\nBrandsville\nMountain View\nWest Plains\nWillow Springs\nElections\nSample Ballots\nHowell County Election Results\nPolling Locations\nStatewide Election Results\nAbsentee Voting Info\nVoters Registration Check\nVoter Registration Information\nCounty Offices\nCommission\nClerk\nCollector\nAssessor\nSheriff\nJury Commission\nCircuit Court Clerk\nRecorder of Deeds\nDirectory\nReport An Issue\nHome\nCities & Towns\nBrandsville\nMountain View\nWest Plains\nWillow Springs\nElections\nSample Ballots\nHowell County Election Results\nPolling Locations\nStatewide Election Results\nAbsentee Voting Info\nVoters Registration Check\nVoter Registration Information\nCounty Offices\nCommission\nClerk\nCollector\nAssessor\nSheriff\nJury Commission\nCircuit Court Clerk\nRecorder of Deeds\nDirectory\nReport An Issues\nRecorder of Deeds\nContact:\n107 Courthouse\nWest Plains MO 65775\n(417) 256-3750\nemail: recorder@howellcountymo.gov\nMarriage License Requirements for Howell County\n$48.00 exact change or a check (No Cards)\nKnow your Social Security number (a card is not required)\nPresent photo I.D.\nIf previously married know the MONTH & YEAR the last marriage ended (no paperwork is required)\nBoth parties must come in between the hours of 8:30 am and 4:00 pm Monday thru Friday\nThe License is good for 30 days anywhere in the state of Missouri, so be within 30 days of the wedding date\nIt usually takes 15 minutes to process and you get the license that same day (no waiting period)\nIf either party is a minor please call for further instructions\nIf you have questions call 417-256-3750\nRecording Fees for Howell County\n$26 for the first page and $3 for all other pages\nRecording Standards\nPlease see RSMO 59.310.5 or call 417-256-3750\nWe also E-file\nHowell County Missouri\nA Great Place to Be!\nQuick Links\nChamber of Commerce 